<!-- ⚠️ PHONE-ONLY 55dp COPY OF ic_pause_48dp. THE ONLY DIFFERENCE FROM THAT FILE IS
     android:width / android:height, 48dp -> 55dp; the viewport, the paths are byte-identical.
     WHY A COPY RATHER THAN AN EDIT: the 48dp set is reached from fragment_player_tv.xml and
     fragment_player_mini_tv.xml through anim_play_pause_48dp, and TV is out of scope. A VectorDrawable
     scales to its BOUNDS, but CompoundButton sizes a button drawable from its INTRINSIC size, and no
     wrapper can raise an intrinsic without shrinking the child by the same amount (InsetDrawable and
     LayerDrawable both move the two in opposite directions) - so the intrinsic has to be declared, and
     that means a file.
     55dp KEEPS THE INK-TO-DISC RATIO THE 56dp DISC HAD: 48/56 = 0.857, and 64 x 0.857 = 54.86.
     ⚠️ KEEP IN STEP WITH ic_pause_48dp. If a path there changes, change it here too; there is no
     include mechanism for vectors. Nothing else in the app should reference the 55dp set - it exists
     for item_player_controls.xml's trackPlayPause alone. -->
